# direnv: drop into the flake's dev shell on `cd`, leave it on the way out.
#
#   brew install direnv   (or: it is already in this fleet's home-manager)
#   direnv allow
#
# There is deliberately NO dotenv chain here. This repository reads no
# environment variable at runtime — the scripts run in a browser — so a
# committed `.env` ladder would be machinery with nothing to carry. Run
# `nix run .#env-doctor` for the short list of variables that DO matter, all of
# them tooling or CI.
use flake

# Per-operator overrides, gitignored, and a SHELL file rather than a dotenv
# one: it can COMPUTE a value instead of storing it, which is how a token stays
# out of the repository entirely. For example:
#
#   export GH_TOKEN="$(security find-generic-password -s gh-token -w)"
source_env_if_exists .envrc.local

# Useful things to put in .envrc.local:
#
#   export USERSCRIPTS_WATCH=0          # stop Claude Code's hooks auto-starting
#                                       # the browser + live-injection loop
#   export USERSCRIPTS_CDP_PORT=9333    # move it off 9222
#   export USERSCRIPTS_CHROME=/path     # use an installed browser, not the pin
